WEBVTT

NOTE
Accessibility audio description for Final Fantasy VIII - Disc 2 (Game Disc 3)
Scene: disc02_09h.avi - Boarding and activating the Ragnarok
Duration: approximately 48 seconds
For blind and low-vision players using screen readers

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
Squall and Rinoa float toward the Ragnarok's airlock. The outer hatch looms large, a circular metal door with safety markings. As they approach, the airlock opens, revealing a dark interior passageway. They enter the ship, crossing the threshold from the lethal vacuum of space into the enclosed environment of the abandoned spacecraft.

00:10.000 --> 00:20.000
The interior of the Ragnarok is dim and oppressive. Dust particles float in the air, visible in faint emergency lighting. The ship has been abandoned and dormant for seventeen years. Squall moves purposefully, carrying Rinoa's still-unconscious body. Together they navigate through narrow corridors lined with sealed doors and equipment panels. Emergency lights cast pale red or amber glows, creating deep shadows. The environment feels alien and uninviting, a tomb of cold metal and silence.

00:20.000 --> 00:30.000
Squall reaches the bridge — a spacious cockpit area that serves as the command center of the Ragnarok. The bridge is expansive, with multiple console stations and a panoramic viewport showing the curve of the planet below. Rinoa's limp form is gently laid on one of the command chairs or a resting place nearby. Squall moves to the main console, his hands moving across panels and switches. Systems begin to respond to his input. Lights flicker on one by one — navigation systems, life support readouts, engine status indicators. The bridge gradually illuminates as power flows through the ship's systems.

00:30.000 --> 00:40.000
The engines of the Ragnarok hum to life, a low vibration resonating through the entire ship. Through the vast panoramic viewport, the planet curves majestically below them. Clouds swirl across its surface, and the deep blues of oceans are visible. Squall watches the viewport, his silhouette framed against the celestial view. The moment is profound — they are no longer drifting helplessly in the void. They have reclaimed control and purpose. The ship responds to its pilots once more, after seventeen years of silence.

00:40.000 --> 00:48.000
Rinoa's eyes flutter open. Her consciousness gradually returns as she awakens from her coma or unconscious state. Squall is there, his attention immediately drawn to her. They share a quiet moment together in the cockpit — no dialogue, only the soft hum of the ship's systems and the distant throb of the engines. The stars and the curved planet are visible through the massive viewport behind them. Through the windows, Earth grows larger and more detailed as the Ragnarok begins its descent. The spacecraft banks slightly, its nose angling toward the planet's atmosphere. They are coming home.
